# API telemetry

The API explicitly owns a Pluto telemetry runtime, request middleware, correlated
JSON logging and a bounded shutdown. The independently versioned
github.com/plutoframework/pluto-core/telemetry module is pinned to v0.1.1.
No global SDK provider or automatic business-operation instrumentation is installed.

Telemetry is disabled by default. Configure it through environment variables
using {{.Prefix}}OTEL_ENABLED=true, {{.Prefix}}OTEL_ENDPOINT=https://collector:4318
and {{.Prefix}}OTEL_SAMPLE_RATIO=1 (a fraction from 0 to 1).
The endpoint uses OTLP over HTTP; standard OTLP exporter settings also apply. Service name defaults to {{.Name}}; service version
defaults to dev (set with Go's -ldflags "-X main.version=v1.2.3").
{{.Prefix}}ENVIRONMENT defaults to development. Settings are read once during
startup. No .env file is loaded. Credentials belong in the secret environment.

The authored cmd/api/telemetry.go is the application customization point.
Review exporter endpoints, transport security and collected attributes before
enabling export. The runtime emits bounded route labels rather than raw request
paths; do not add credentials, bodies or arbitrary user identifiers as attributes.
The API flushes telemetry after stopping HTTP service. The worker owns a separate runtime with the
same environment settings, service name {{.Name}}-worker and its own dev version.
It wraps registered job handlers and its pgx pool, then flushes on bounded shutdown.
Durable jobs start new trace roots; incoming context is not persisted in the outbox.

The API wraps app.Dependencies.Cache and configures pgx query tracing before pool
creation. Cache keys/values and SQL text/parameters are omitted. Existing Open and
NewWorker callers remain compatible and opt out of instrumentation by default.

Existing generated applications must adopt these authored files and composition
changes deliberately; adding an endpoint never overwrites them.
